# ============================================================
# Human-owned paths of the AI factory (backlog #0-113). With "Require review from Code Owners" on in the
# branch protection of main, a PR touching any of these waits for the owner's approval; every other PR
# can merge on green checks alone (the autopilot's --auto merge).
#
# The owner must be a login GitHub can resolve: it ignores lines whose owner it cannot, and then nothing
# is protected. While the autopilot pushes with the owner's own account (shadow mode without the machine
# account of #0-113), leave "Require review from Code Owners" off: GitHub does not let an author approve
# their own pull request, so every autopilot PR touching these paths could never merge. With the rule off,
# this file enforces nothing: the paths below are guarded only by the autopilot's path gate
# (scripts/factory/changed-paths.sh) and by the owner reading each PR before merging it.
# ============================================================

# What the agents are judged by, and their own configuration
